    "nci_treatment": "None material; flows are 100% attributable.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (routing table: mature US operating company; cyclical industrial - freight volumes track industrial production/trade, so no WACC premium but a 20% bear weight and a cap below Gordon). Not a REIT/bank/holdco. STANDALONE UNP: the pending ~$85B Norfolk Southern acquisition (announced 2025-07-29; STB procedural schedule adopted 2026-08-18; targeted close late 2027; opposed by BNSF, CSX, shipper coalitions, labor, farm groups, DOJ Antitrust) is not modelled - no NS revenue, synergies, ~225M new shares, ~$20B+ acquisition debt or assumed NS debt. If it closes, the leverage and share-count inputs here are superseded and the valuation must be rebuilt on a combined basis. Merger agreement carries a reverse termination fee payable by UNP on regulatory failure (reported ~$2.5B, ~$4/share; not verified against the filing here, not in the bridge). Buybacks: historically a large repurchaser ($2.7B FY25, $6-8B/yr FY18-22) but effectively paused since the NS announcement ($26M H1-26) - the flat count is currently a modelling convention, not being funded. Other income ($629M FY25: real-estate sales, rents, pension credit) is excluded from the flows and no matching asset is added - a conservative omission of roughly $0.5B/yr. Owner FCF = reported FCF $5,499M - SBC $142M - interest income 0 (net-debt company, no deduction). Reported FCF is after ~$1.3B interest; the engine projects unlevered FCF and deducts net debt once.",
